 110:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     [..]
 111:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     By default, after the HAL_USART_Init() and when the state is HAL_USART_STATE_RESET
 112:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 113:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     examples HAL_USART_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_USART_RxHalfCpltCallback().
 114:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are respectively
 115:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_USART_Init()
 116:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     and HAL_USART_DeInit() only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 117:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_USART_Init() and HAL_USART_DeInit()
 118:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand).
 119:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c **** 
 120:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     [..]
 121:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_USART_STATE_READY state only.
 122:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 123:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     in HAL_USART_STATE_READY or HAL_USART_STATE_RESET state, thus registered (user)
 124:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 125:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 126:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     using HAL_USART_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_USART_DeInit()
 127:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     or HAL_USART_Init() function.
 128:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c **** 
 129:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     [..]
 130:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_USART_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 131:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     not defined, the callback registration feature is not available
 132:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_usart.c ****     and weak callbacks are used.
